+Column2: shove recovery, right hand withdrawing and shoulders sagging breathlessly; left phone still held.
+Column3: hit/flinch initial recoil, one shoulder jerked back, eyes squeezed, knees flexed, right hand startled open, phone still in left.
+Column4: stronger hit/flinch crumple, belly and shoulders hunch, knees buckle, right arm protective; phone retained left. No gore/blood.
+Column5: FALL starts, off-balance backwards stumble, tilted torso and arms trying to balance, phone retained.
+Column6: FALL midway, knees collapse, torso much lower and tipped to side/back; clearly falling.
+Column7: FULLY DOWN lying still on side/back, whole torso/hair/face/arms/phone/legs horizontal or diagonal ON GROUND, NOT kneeling or standing. The body is compactly curled/folded to fit48x64. This is an unmistakably fallen person silhouette, head low beside torso, knees bent, belly round and blacktee clear. Full body inside cell, no cut limbs or head. Keep identity readable. Phone clutched in left hand. No detached parts, no gore, no floor shadow. Orient fallen body according to row facing, but side curl may keep it compact.
+CRITICAL: these are32 actually different ACTION poses, NOT repeating idle/walk sprites. The final three frames must visibly progress from standing stumble to collapse to lying on ground in EACH row. Keep exact hair/body/costume design and scale across poses. Original gritty deliberate low-resolution pixel drawings compatible with reference1. Shared controlled31-color palette: purple-nearblack outlines/hair/blacktee, warm tan skin flat ramps, dark bluegrey trousers, restrained cyan/magenta highlights, tiny cyan phone screen. No photographic texture, smooth paintings, diffuse glow, white matte, shadow, background, checkerboard, grid lines, labels, text, UI, watermark, scenery or extra characters. Outside sprite alpha must be zero.
